---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PaintCostCalculator from '../../components/PaintCostCalculator.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Room Paint Calculator: Gallons and Cost"
  description="Free room paint calculator: enter room size, doors, windows and coats to get gallons needed, DIY cost and a rough professional price range."
>
  <h1>Room paint calculator</h1>
  <p>
    Enter your room size, the number of doors and windows and how many coats you plan to apply. The
    calculator returns the gallons to buy, the DIY cost and a rough professional labor range. No
    sign-up, and nothing you type leaves your browser.
  </p>

  <PaintCostCalculator length={12} width={12} height={8} doors={1} windows={2} />

  <h2>How the estimate works</h2>
  <p>
    Wall area is the room's perimeter times the ceiling height. The tool subtracts openings (our guides
    use about 20 sq ft per door and 15 per window), multiplies by the number of coats, and divides by
    the coverage of a gallon. Sources we cite put that at about 350 to 400 sq ft per coat on smooth,
    primed walls, and the figure printed on your can is the one to trust. The result is rounded up to
    whole containers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Texture, bare drywall and big color changes use more paint, and primer covers less per gallon than
    paint. Professional labor is a rough range, not a quote: get written quotes before you hire anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Related guides</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/how-much-paint-do-i-need/">How much paint do I need? Formula and worked examples</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/cost-to-paint-a-room/">Cost to paint a room</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/cost-to-paint-trim-and-baseboards/">Cost to paint trim and baseboards</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/paint-roller-vs-sprayer-cost/">Paint roller vs sprayer cost</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
